<title>INDIA: India's CMIE sees '96/97 farm growth up at 4.7 pct.</title>
<headline>India's CMIE sees '96/97 farm growth up at 4.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's agricultural production is expected to sharply rise by 4.7 percent in 1996/97 (April-March) from a negative 0.2 percent in the previous year, the Centre for Monitoring Indian Economy said.  </p>
<p>CMIE, a Bombay-based independent think-tank, in a review of the Indian economy made available to Reuters on Wednesday, projected 1996/97 foodgrains production higher at 196.3 million tonnes against 185 million in the previous year.</p>
